# NeoDev Git DocChange

Before every Git commit, classify staged files:

```bash
python plugins/neodev-rd-knowledge/check_git_commit_scope.py
```

Document-only commits must complete the document workflow first:

```bash
neodev doc binding list --product-code <product_code> --json
neodev doc binding create --product-code <product_code> --version-name <version_name> --project-id <doc_project_id> --branch <branch> --json
neodev doc import --doc-binding-id <doc_binding_id> --json
neodev doc change register --document-id <document_id> --json
```

Document identity is scoped by product version. The unique key is `doc_id + product_version_id`; re-importing the same `doc_id` in the same version overwrites that version's document record, but never another version's record.

Code commits must include exactly one trailer:

```text
DocChange-ID: 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
```

The value must be the 40-character Git commit hash of the imported source document.

Validate commit messages with:

```bash
python plugins/neodev-rd-knowledge/check_docchange_trailer.py --message-file .git/COMMIT_EDITMSG
```

Before push, verify through the local `neodev` CLI client against the configured remote service:

```bash
neodev config show
neodev cli version-check --json
neodev git verify-doc-change --project-id <project_id> --branch <branch> --commit-sha <commit_sha> --commit-message <commit_message> --json
```

Mixed document and code commits are not allowed; split them so the correct workflow is unambiguous.

After a successful `git push`, do not run separate document import, DocChange registration, code-link, or graph-refresh commands. The post-push hook runs the single server-side atomic update:

```bash
neodev git post-push-graph-update --payload-file <local_payload_file> --json
```

Interpret the hook result and only report manual recovery when the structured payload says `rollback_status=rollback_failed`.

If verification reports dangerous commits, explain the structured payload and require explicit user confirmation before resolving or continuing.
